<title>ITALY: Italy's Bologna sees March CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bologna sees March CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>BOLOGNA, Italy 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bologna said its February consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 2.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In February, Bologna's inflation rate was flat and 2.6 percent respectively. The general index and housing and utility charges sector have been revised to take account of a court ruling last month that suspended electricity tariff reductions.</p>
<p>Bologna is one of 11 Italian cities to publish inflation data Thursday and Friday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.62 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to February 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0    (0.0R)   2.3    (2.6R)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.6   (-0.1)   -0.8    (0.0)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.6    (0.0)    2.5    (2.5)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.2    (0.4R)   7.3    (7.2R)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.2   (-0.4)    1.3    (1.2)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2    (1.3)    6.0    (5.8)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.3    (0.3)    1.4    (1.9)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.3   (-1.1)    5.3    (5.8)</p>
<p>    Education			  -0.3    (0.4)    2.4    (2.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0    (0.3)    1.9    (2.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2    (0.2)    1.3    (1.2)</p>
<p>R - revised</p>
